  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The external finishing materials shall match those used in the construction of the existing building and/or areas of hard surfacing. \rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r2509-03-02 A, 2509-03-01 A, 2509-03-03 A, 2509-03-05 A, 2509-03-04 A, 2509-03-06 A, Energy statement, Highway Impact assessment   \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    ": Prior to occupation, unless otherwise agreed cycle parking should be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\roProvision of a minimum of FOUR long stay cycle parking spaces (two per unit)\roin an accessible location: the access route to each long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m\rosecured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob\rofully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof\r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation details of the design of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site, shall be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield - Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance ENV 08/162.\rIn particular, waste collection vehicles must be able to get within 25m of the refuse storage point. Residents should not have to carry waste further than 30m.\r\rReason: In order to facilitate efficient, safe and clean removal of household refuse, the location and accessibility of refuse storage plus to maintain safety on the Highway.\r"
  ],
